    {
      "id": "5157acdd-cc1d-4f25-88d6-9ee47413e9b4",
      "name": "Why MCP Makes Software Feel Alive",
      "path": "WWW / MCP Field Notes / Why MCP Makes Software Feel Alive",
      "docTypeId": "162d98a7-72a5-4b97-8b96-b60b5c4123ec",
      "templateId": "97b6167c-fe23-4820-95a7-32a0acd15aef",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "59bee277-5312-438c-a7fb-7dde3ee744f2",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "c8879acb-c929-4d04-95eb-e218d52bd7f1",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "3e37b39f-032b-4439-8639-d68175d47817",
                "key": "59bee277-5312-438c-a7fb-7dde3ee744f2",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "eyebrow",
                    "value": "PROTOCOLS & POSSIBILITIES"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "heading",
                    "value": "Why MCP makes software feel alive"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "introduction",
                    "value": "MCP gives an AI assistant a clear, inspectable way to work with the tools and data already living on your machine."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "00591338-82eb-4bee-95f4-42879362c969",
                        "mediaKey": "8e8abce6-9275-4183-8028-9f726ccf4df8",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "imageAltText",
                    "value": "Colourful source code filling a computer screen"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "imageCredit",
                    "value": "Photo by Chris Ried on Unsplash"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "66b8e626-0891-49d4-b02c-cf25325c3829",
                "key": "c8879acb-c929-4d04-95eb-e218d52bd7f1",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>Most software tools wait for us to learn their menus, APIs, and conventions. The Model Context Protocol flips that relationship around: it gives an assistant a structured map of what a system can do, then lets the assistant combine those capabilities around an outcome.</p><h2>A shared language for useful work</h2><p>MCP tools are explicit. A content command describes the fields it accepts. A read operation returns structured data. An error can explain exactly which assumption failed. That shared language turns a vague request into a sequence of actions that both people and software can inspect.</p><p>On this site, the protocol did more than answer questions. It inspected the existing Umbraco structure, created element types, configured a Block Grid, imported local media, and published this article. Each step used the same management surface an editor or integration would trust.</p><h2>Power with boundaries</h2><p>The best automation is not magic. It is powerful because its boundaries are visible. MCP makes allowed operations discoverable, encourages typed inputs, and keeps the host application in charge of validation and permissions.</p><blockquote><p>The exciting part is not that an assistant can click faster. It is that intent can meet a well-defined capability without losing the rules of the system.</p></blockquote><h2>Composable by design</h2><p>A small tool can become part of a much larger workflow. Schema inspection, media upload, content creation, and verification remain separate capabilities, but MCP lets them cooperate. That makes integrations easier to evolve and far easier to reason about than one giant opaque automation script.</p><p>When software can clearly describe what it knows and what it can do, it stops feeling like a collection of closed boxes. It starts feeling like a living workspace.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "59bee277-5312-438c-a7fb-7dde3ee744f2",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "c8879acb-c929-4d04-95eb-e218d52bd7f1",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
