    {
      "id": "65cc90a0-8ac3-48d2-a6bd-bed718fe1f32",
      "name": "Local MCP Is a Developer Superpower",
      "path": "WWW / MCP Field Notes / Local MCP Is a Developer Superpower",
      "docTypeId": "162d98a7-72a5-4b97-8b96-b60b5c4123ec",
      "templateId": "97b6167c-fe23-4820-95a7-32a0acd15aef",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "blocks",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "6a882ebf-8cdb-492f-85a0-71fcd8cbcd2c",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "f03dbcd7-1f6c-4516-aede-9b75efd3f84d",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "3e37b39f-032b-4439-8639-d68175d47817",
                "key": "6a882ebf-8cdb-492f-85a0-71fcd8cbcd2c",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "eyebrow",
                    "value": "LOCAL-FIRST WORKFLOWS"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "heading",
                    "value": "Local MCP is a developer superpower"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "introduction",
                    "value": "A local MCP server collapses the distance between an idea, the real application, and a verified result—without skipping the project’s rules."
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "9e2e8882-8aa9-4c08-8ebb-9500715b7093",
                        "mediaKey": "c31ace9e-7c01-4828-8277-7888bc162fbb",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "imageAltText",
                    "value": "Two people fitting wooden puzzle pieces together"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "imageCredit",
                    "value": "Photo by Vardan Papikyan on Unsplash"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "66b8e626-0891-49d4-b02c-cf25325c3829",
                "key": "f03dbcd7-1f6c-4516-aede-9b75efd3f84d",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "body",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>Fast feedback changes how we build. When an assistant can talk to the local application through MCP, it can inspect the real schema, use the real validation pipeline, and immediately read its work back. That is a much richer loop than generating a pile of files and hoping they line up later.</p><h2>The application stays the source of truth</h2><p>This blog was created through Umbraco itself. Document types live in the prescribed folders. Media sits inside a media folder. Pages use the project’s root repository and routing convention. The Block Grid payloads were accepted, published, and read back by the running CMS.</p><p>That matters because local automation should reinforce architecture rather than route around it. The server owns identifiers, validation, persistence, and publishing state. The assistant orchestrates those capabilities while the application remains authoritative.</p><h2>Feedback arrives while context is fresh</h2><p>A local MCP loop can catch mistakes at the point they happen: a missing required value, an invalid content type, a malformed block key, or a write that did not survive serialization. Each read-back narrows uncertainty before the next step begins.</p><ul><li>Inspect before creating.</li><li>Use typed tools instead of guessing endpoints.</li><li>Read structural writes back immediately.</li><li>Build rendering only after the content model is settled.</li></ul><h2>Automation that respects craft</h2><p>Speed is useful, but the deeper win is continuity. The same workflow can honor naming, folders, rendering conventions, image handling, and deployment artifacts while still moving quickly. The protocol provides leverage without erasing the decisions that make a codebase coherent.</p><p>That combination—local context, explicit capabilities, and rapid verification—is why MCP feels less like a shortcut and more like a genuine developer superpower.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "6a882ebf-8cdb-492f-85a0-71fcd8cbcd2c",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "f03dbcd7-1f6c-4516-aede-9b75efd3f84d",
                "culture": null,
